{"adaptation_by": [], "sections": [{"content": [{"page_number": 1, "type": "stage_direction", "description": "1/ PROLOG\nALLE (Stimme vom Band)", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Who am I?", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "I am in a strange state of mind.", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "I am alone", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "quite alone", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "in the world", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "who is the other of my thoughts?", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "I know that I am about", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "to die /to be born", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "and I feel happy", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "joyous", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "I feel my pulse; it beats fast:", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "I place my thin hand on my cheek; it burns:", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "there is a slight, quick spirit within me which is now\nemitting its first", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "its last sparks", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "a feeling that I cannot define leads me on", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "I am a creature", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "and I am too weak both in body and mind to resist the slightest impulse", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "the impulse to create", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "the impulse to destroy", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "I may tread a land never before imprinted by the foot of man", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 1, "type": "dialogue", "line": "I must collect my thoughts", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "there is something at work in my soul that I do not understand", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Am I not alone?", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "I must pursue and destroy the being to whom I gave existence", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "then my lot on earth will be fulfilled and I may die", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "I walk a little offroad", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Old borders collapse", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "new ones are being drawn", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Dangerous", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Liberating", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Where is the ultimate border?", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "\"A little patience, and all will be over.\"", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Who am I?", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "stage_direction", "description": "dt. Übersetzung", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Wer bin ich?", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ich bin in einer merkwürdigen Gemütsverfassung", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ich bin allein", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ziemlich allein", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "In der Welt", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "wer ist der Autor meiner Gedanken", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ich weiß ich bin kurz davor", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "zu sterben", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "geboren zu werden", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "und ich bin glücklich", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 2, "type": "dialogue", "line": "fröhlich", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ich fühle meinen Puls; er schlägt schnell", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ich lege meine dünne Hand auf meine Wange; sie brennt", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Da ist ein leichter, flüchtiger Geist in mir, der seine\nersten Strahlen aussendet", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "seine letzten", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ein Gefühl, das ich nicht definieren kann, leitet mich", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "und ich bin körperlich und geistig zu schwach, um dem geringsten Impuls zu widerstehen", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "dem Impuls zu erschaffen", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "dem Impuls zu zerstören", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "ich werde meinen Fuß auf ein Land setzen, das vor mir noch nie jemand betreten hat", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ich muss meine Gedanken ordnen", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "irgendetwas, das ich nicht verstehe, arbeitet in meiner Seele", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Bin ich nicht allein?", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ich muss das Wesen, dem ich seine Existenz geschenkt habe, verfolgen und zerstören", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Dann wird mein Schicksal auf Erden erfüllt sein und ich kann sterben", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "I walk a little offroad", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Old borders collapse", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "new ones are being drawn", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Dangerous", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Liberating", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 3, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Wo ist die ultimative Grenze?", "scene_number": "1", "scene_title": "PROLOG", "speaker": "ALLE"}, {"page_number": 4, "type": "stage_direction", "description": "2 / DER TOD, MARY ERFINDET EINE SCHAUERGESCHICHTE\nMaren, Felix und Alexander in der Ur-Form/Homo Sapiens", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD"}, {"page_number": 4, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Menschen sterben. Der Tod ist ein zu schrecklicher Gegenstand. Menschen\nvertragen nicht sehr viel Realität. Deshalb erfinden wir Geschichten.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 4, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Und was, wenn wir die Geschichten sind, die wir erfinden?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 4, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Schon als Kind war es meine Lieblingsbeschäftigung, in den Stunden, die ich mir selbst\nüberlassen war, Geschichten zu erzählen. Doch ich machte mich nicht zur Heldin\nmeiner Geschichte(n). Ich war nicht auf meine eigene Identität angewiesen und\nkonnte die Stunden mit Schöpfungen bevölkern, die viel interessanter für mich waren\nals meine eigenen Empfindungen. -", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 4, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Verdiene ich es nicht, Großes zu vollbringen?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 4, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Meine Stimmungen und meine Leidenschaften sind zuweilen heftig.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 4, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Aber durch irgendein inneres Gesetz meines Wesens werden sie umgewandelt in den\nunbedingten Wunsch zu lernen.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 4, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Diese Geschichte kann als die Erfahrung gelesen werden, diese Geschichte zu\nerzählen", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 4, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Es sind die Geheimnisse des Himmels und der Erde, die ich ergründen will.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 4, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Woraus geht das Prinzip des Lebens hervor?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 4, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Um die Ursache des Lebens zu untersuchen, müssen wir uns erst mit dem Tod\nbeschäftigen.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 4, "type": "joint_dialogue", "lines": ["Meine Mutter starb friedlich."], "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speakers": ["ALEXANDER", "MAREN"]}, {"page_number": 4, "type": "dialogue", "line": "A little patience and it will all be over.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 4, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Und selbst im Tod sprach noch Liebe aus ihren Zügen.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 4, "type": "dialogue", "line": "The memory of my mother has always been the pride and delight of my life. Sie starb\nbei meiner Geburt. Ich lernte lesen mit meinem Finger auf der Inschrift ihres Grabes.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 4, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Für meinen Vater war sie die Größte.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Und nach ihrem Tod setzte er seine Hoffnung in mich. Ich bin Mary, die\nNamensvetterin meiner Mutter, der großen Frauenrechtlerin und das\nNamenssouvenir meines Vaters.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ich brauche das Gefühl nicht zu beschreiben.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Das Gefühl derer, deren liebste Bindungen von", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "- dem irreparabelsten aller Übel zerrissen werden.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Die Leere, die sich der Seele offenbart.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Die Verzweiflung, die sich auf dem Gesicht zeigt.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Trauer ist das Gefühl mit jemandem zu leben, der nicht mehr da ist.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Glaubst du an Geister?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Wie könnte der Körper Herr über den Geist sein? Unser Mut, unsere\nHeldenhaftigkeit, selbst unser Hass, alles was wir tun, um die Welt zu formen, ist das\nder Körper oder der Geist?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Es ist der Geist.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Von meiner Schöpfung und meinem Schöpfer wusste ich absolut nichts.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "War ich ein Monster?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ich fing an, Bücher zu lesen;", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "-mich mehr mit den Gedanken anderer zu identifizieren; meine Individualität in der\nMenge derer zu verlieren, die vor mir existiert hatten.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Aber mein Kummer nahm mit dem Wissen zu.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Oh, wären die Menschen für immer in ihren heimischen Wäldern geblieben! Oh,\nhätten wir nichts anderes gekannt außer dem Gefühl von Hunger, Durst und Hitze.\nVon welch seltsamer Natur Wissen ist.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Wenn es einem Menschen je gelänge, einen Toten wiederzubeleben, durch\nGalvanismus oder sonst eine bislang unentdeckte Methode, würde der Geist dann\nzurückkehren?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Wieso sollte der Geist in ein ruiniertes Haus zurückkehren?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 5, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Nichts trägt so sehr zur Beruhigung des Geistes bei wie ein beharrlich verfolgtes Ziel.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ein Fixpunkt, auf den die Seele ihr geistiges Auge richten kann.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "\"Hast Du Dir schon eine Geschichte ausgedacht, Mary?\" fragte Byron. Nichts kommt,\nwenn es gerufen wird man muss demütig zugeben, dass das Neue nicht aus dem\nNichts kreiert wird.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Sondern aus dem Chaos.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Es war das Jahr ohne Sommer, eine Naturkatastrophe verdunkelte die Welt.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ich werde meine Wissensgier befriedigen und meinen Fuß auf ein Land setzen, dass\nvor mir noch niemand betreten hat.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Was würde dich am meisten ängstigen?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ewiges Leben. Diese Verlockung reicht aus, um all meine Furcht vor Gefahr und Tod\nzu besiegen.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Nein, ich möchte nicht ewig leben, das Leben ist schon quälend genug.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Was ich will, existiert, wenn ich wage, es zu finden.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Everything you can think of is true.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ich erzähle eine Geschichte. Eine Geschichte, die macht, dass es dem Leser davor\ngraut, sich umzublicken, die das Blut gerinnen lässt und die Schläge des Herzens\nbeschleunigt.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Es genügt nicht, die Natur und die Wahrheit zu erforschen. Man muss auch den Mut\nhaben, davon zu erzählen.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Benennen bedeutet Macht.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Wer Dinge falsch benennt, trägt zum Unheil der Welt bei.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Eine Geschichte, die unsere geheimnisvollen, menschlichen Urängste anspricht und\ntiefes Entsetzen weckt. Einerseits dient das Gedankenspiel der Unterhaltung,\nandererseits trägt es dazu bei, in unerforschte Regionen des Geistes vorzudringen.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Jede Sache muss einen Anfang haben. Und dieser Anfang muss mit etwas verbunden\nsein, das davor geschah.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 6, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Unser erstes Kind starb kurz nach seiner Geburt. Der Tod ist natürlich. Verfall\nunumgänglich. Ich bin den Tod gewöhnt, und ich hasse ihn. Es gibt kein neues Leben\nohne Tod. Es kann keinen Tod geben, solange es kein Leben gibt. Kein Leben ohne", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Tod, kein Tod ohne Leben, kein...", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Kann ich sterben?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Das Wesen der Sterblichkeit und Endlichkeit und das Wesen der Sprache\nverschwören sich immer wieder, um uns zum Stottern zu bringen.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Man kann niemals das haben, worauf man nicht verzichten kann.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Man stolpert immer genau dann, wenn man glaubt, am Ziel zu sein.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Meiner Geschichte wegen habe ich den Wunsch herauszufinden, was uns Menschen\nvom Rest des biologischen Lebens unterscheidet.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Und was von Maschinen.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "So vieles wurde bereits erreicht...", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "... rief die Seele Frankensteins aus", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "aber mehr, viel mehr habe ich vor zu erreichen;", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "FRANKENSTEIN, ich nenne meine Geschichte “Frankenstein”.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Fehlt da nicht was?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Was denn, soll ich sie Viktor Frankenstein nennen?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Nein, deine Geschichte ist mehr als nur seine Geschichte? Sind es nicht Zwei, die\nineinander Leben? Frankenstein im Monster?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Das Monster in Frankenstein?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ja, und - deshalb hat das Monster keinen Namen, es braucht ihn nicht.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Wer gibt seinem Kind keinen Namen?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Wer entsetzt ist, über das, was er geschaffen hat.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ich bin Vater und Mutter der Geschichte, es ist meine Schöpfung.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ich weiß, dass ich das Ding, das mich umtreibt verleugne, indem ich es nicht benenne.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Doch welchen Namen soll man einer neuen Schöpfung geben?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 7, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ich, Viktor Frankenstein, werde über die vorgezeichneten Bahnen hinaus\nneue Wege einschlagen, unbekannte Kräfte erforschen und der Welt die tiefsten\nGeheimnisse der Schöpfung offenbaren.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 8, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Geschichte ist das, wozu man sie macht.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 8, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Wir sind die Geschichte, die wir machen.", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 8, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Warum hast du mich verlassen?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "FELIX"}, {"page_number": 8, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Mein Vater verstieß mich, \n-als ich so zu leben und zu lieben begann, wie er und\nwie meine Mutter es in ihren Büchern propagiert hatten. Meine Mutter...was würde\nmeine Mutter sagen, wenn ich sie von den Toten zurückholen könnte? Das Herz einer\nFrau, was ist das? Der Geist einer Frau, was ist das? Hat man uns im innersten Kern\nanders gemacht? Oder beruht Andersartigkeit nur auf Sitte und Macht?", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "MAREN"}, {"page_number": 8, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Ich, Offenbarer eines neuen Menschen. Sehen sie sich die Götter an, die wir uns\nbereits ausgedacht haben, egal ob griechisch, römisch, indisch oder ägyptisch,\nbabylonisch oder aztekisch, aus Ragnarök oder Wallhalla, Wesen der Unterwelt oder\ndes sternbesetzten Himmels: sie sind verbesserte Menschen; - sie haben unsere\nGelüste, Fehden und Begierden,", "scene_number": "2", "scene_title": "DER TOD", "speaker": "ALEXANDER"}, {"page_number": 8, "type": "dialogue", "line": "Gefühle", "scene_number": "2", "scene